<odoo>
    <!--
        The shipped catalogue seed.

        WHY THESE 30 LIBRARIES
        ======================
        Chosen for Vertel's customers — hosting, ERP and integration work — not
        by upstream popularity. The groups, in order:

          * Cloud architecture (6): AWS serverless, AWS architecture, Azure,
            GCP, Google icons, cloud design patterns.
          * Architecture and modelling (6): C4, hexagonal, software
            architecture, architecture diagram components, enterprise
            integration patterns, message queue components.
          * UML and process (4): UML & ER shapes, UML component diagram, BPMN,
            flow chart symbols.
          * Network and infrastructure (5): network topology, network elements,
            network locations, fibre network, racks and servers.
          * Data and system design (3): database, system design components,
            data flow.
          * Facilities and shop floor (2): architecture floor plan symbols,
            P&ID.
          * Development and UI (4): dev ops icons, technology logos,
            wireframing placeholders, decision flow control.

        DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED: DnD, football, chickens, biology, math teacher.
        They are fine libraries; they are not what a customer draws an
        integration diagram with.

        WHY THE FILES ARE COMMITTED
        ===========================
        `source_url` points at the module's own static path, so a fresh install
        has a browsable catalogue with NO network access (spec: "A fresh
        install has a browsable catalogue"). Sync is opt-in and separate.

        The files were fetched 2026-11-05 from
        raw.githubusercontent.com/excalidraw/excalidraw-libraries/main/libraries/
        and are MIT-licensed by their authors; the author and licence position
        is in the `authors` field of each record.

        ⚠️ A THIRD OF THESE ARE FORMAT v1
        =================================
        10 of the 30 are `version: 1` with a `library` key (a list of bare
        element arrays) instead of `version: 2` with `libraryItems`. Both load
        in Excalidraw 0.18.1 — its own loader migrates v1 — but the module's
        parser must accept both or a third of the catalogue is invisible.
        See `_parse_library` in models/dms_excalidraw_library.py.

        `noupdate="1"`: an upgrade must not resurrect a library an
        administrator deliberately archived, and must not overwrite an edited
        `source_url`.
    -->
